.TH XPROXY.YAML 5 "" "Xproxy" "File formats"
.nh
.ad l
.SH "NAME"
.PP
xproxy.yaml \- configuration of xproxy
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
\fB/etc/xproxy/xproxy.yaml\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
xproxy reads one YAML document. Unknown keys are errors. Every omitted value takes the default listed here; a zero duration or count means "default", never "disabled". Paths must be absolute. Durations use Go syntax: \fB500ms\fR, \fB10s\fR, \fB5m\fR, \fB1h\fR. Names match \fB[A\-Za\-z0\-9][A\-Za\-z0\-9_.\-]{0,63}\fR.
.PP
Validate with \fBxproxy \-config FILE \-validate\fR; all problems are reported at once. The example in \fBdeploy/config/xproxy.yaml\fR exercises most keys.
.PP
This reference is also installed as the manual page \fBxproxy.yaml(5)\fR, and a JSON schema generated from the same types (\fB/usr/share/xproxy/xproxy.schema.json\fR, \fBxproxyctl schema\fR) gives editors completion and inline documentation; put \fB# yaml\-language\-server: $schema=/usr/share/xproxy/xproxy.schema.json\fR on the first line of the file to enable it.
.SH "Top level"
.PP
