.SS "logging.siem"
.PP
Ships log records to a security information and event management system over HTTPS: Splunk\(aqs HTTP Event Collector, Elastic and OpenSearch ingest endpoints, Microsoft Sentinel\(aqs data collector, or any receiver of newline delimited JSON, CEF or LEEF. Records queue without blocking the request path, a full queue drops and counts, and a batching goroutine posts by size and interval and flushes at shutdown, the same way the \fBotlp\fR sink works. Redaction runs before the sink. \fBxproxyctl telemetry\fR and \fBGET /v1/telemetry\fR show the counters, \fBxproxyctl status\fR \fBlog_siem_sent\fR and \fBlog_siem_dropped\fR, and the metrics \fBxproxy_log_sent_total{sink="siem"}\fR and \fBxproxy_log_dropped_total{sink="siem"}\fR.
.PP
Formats:
.RS 3n
.PP
.ti -3n
\(bu
\fBjson\fR: one JSON line per record, \fBapplication/x\-ndjson\fR, the line every other sink sees (with \fBstream\fR).
.PP
.ti -3n
\(bu
\fBhec\fR: the Splunk HTTP Event Collector envelope per record (\fBtime\fR, \fBhost\fR, \fBsource: xproxy\fR, \fBsourcetype: xproxy:<stream>\fR, \fBevent\fR holding the JSON object), \fBapplication/json\fR; put \fBSplunk <token>\fR in \fBauth_file\fR.
.PP
.ti -3n
\(bu
\fBcef\fR: ArcSight Common Event Format, a header of the vendor, product, version, event id (\fBstream\fR or \fBstream:action\fR), name and severity followed by the extension. Severity is 1, 3 or 5 for access lines by status class, 7 for security events (8 for bans), 3 for audit and 2, 4 or 6 for the error stream by level. Extensions use the standard keys where one exists (\fBrt\fR, \fBdvchost\fR, \fBcat\fR, \fBoutcome\fR, \fBsuser\fR from the identified user, \fBsrc\fR, \fBdst\fR and \fBdpt\fR from the upstream endpoint, \fBrequestMethod\fR, \fBdhost\fR, \fBrequest\fR, \fBrequestClientApplication\fR, \fBrequestContext\fR, \fBapp\fR, \fBin\fR, \fBout\fR, \fBact\fR, \fBreason\fR, \fBmsg\fR), the labelled custom fields for \fBstatus\fR (\fBcn1\fR), \fBduration_ms\fR (\fBcn2\fR), \fBattempts\fR (\fBcn3\fR), \fBrequest_id\fR (\fBcs1\fR), \fBroute\fR (\fBcs2\fR), \fBupstream\fR (\fBcs3\fR), \fBcountry\fR (\fBcs4\fR), \fBja4\fR (\fBcs5\fR) and \fBdetail\fR (\fBcs6\fR), and every other attribute under its own name. Header fields escape \fB|\fR and \fB\e\fR, extension values \fB=\fR, \fB\e\fR and line breaks.
.PP
.ti -3n
\(bu
\fBleef\fR: IBM QRadar Log Event Extended Format 2.0 with a tab delimiter (\fBx09\fR in the header) and the same header fields except name and severity, followed by \fBdevTime\fR, \fBdevTimeFormat\fR, \fBsev\fR, \fBcat\fR, \fBidentHostName\fR, \fBusrName\fR, \fBdst\fR, \fBdstPort\fR, \fBname\fR for non access events, then \fBsrc\fR, \fBurl\fR, \fBproto\fR, \fBuserAgent\fR, \fBreason\fR, \fBaction\fR, \fBmsg\fR and the remaining attributes under their own names.
.RE
.PP
.PP
.TS
