.PP
The fallback keeps a limit from being avoided by omitting the identifier; rotating it still buys fresh buckets, so pair an identifier key with a \fBclient_ip\fR or \fBclient_net\fR policy on the same route. An \fBidentity\fR key cannot be rotated within one authenticated principal: the value is what the \fBjwt\fR, \fBoidc\fR, \fBapi_key\fR or \fBbasic\fR filter verified, so a per\-account or per\-API\-key limit holds regardless of the headers a client sends. Attach such a policy to a route that also runs the matching auth filter (or the \fBjwt\fR route setting); a request that fails authentication is refused by the filter before the limiter.
.PP
Memory: at most 64 x 8192 buckets per policy.
