.SH "ingress"
.PP
Kubernetes ingress controller mode. When enabled, the proxy reads the Ingress, Service, EndpointSlice and TLS Secret resources of one ingress class, and the Gateway API resources (Gateway, HTTPRoute) of the same class when the cluster has them, from the API server with the pod\(aqs service account (no client library), translates them and appends the result to this file\(aqs routes, upstreams and certificates: the running configuration is the file plus the cluster. The file\(aqs own routes and upstreams are kept and a name collision is an error. Watch streams on the resources trigger a sync within \fBdebounce\fR of a change, with a full poll every \fBresync\fR as the fallback; a change reloads the proxy like a SIGHUP, and a SIGHUP or \fBxproxyctl reload\fR re\-reads the file and merges the latest snapshot. The API server being unreachable at start is a warning, not a failure: the file configuration serves until the first successful sync.
.PP
.TS
