.PP
Translation: every \fBrules[].http.paths[]\fR entry becomes a route named \fBk8s\-<namespace>\-<ingress>\-<n>\fR with the rule\(aqs host, the path as a prefix (\fBpathType: Exact\fR gets priority 10 so it wins over a prefix of the same length; \fBImplementationSpecific\fR paths with wildcards are skipped with a warning), and an upstream \fBk8s\-<namespace>\-<service>\-<port>\fR whose endpoints are the ready addresses of the service\(aqs EndpointSlices on the port the service maps to (a service without ready endpoints gets an unreachable placeholder so the route answers 503 rather than disappearing). \fBdefaultBackend\fR becomes a hostless \fB/\fR route with priority \-100; only the first Ingress with one counts. Annotations with the prefix \fBxproxy.sysctl.se/\fR set route options: \fBwebsocket\fR (\fB"true"\fR), \fBpriority\-class\fR, \fBrate\-limits\fR and \fBfilters\fR (comma separated names from this file), \fBtimeout\fR, \fBmax\-body\-bytes\fR, \fBstrip\-prefix\fR (\fB"true"\fR strips the matched path), \fBhost\-header\fR. Names over 64 bytes are shortened with a digest.
.PP
Gateway API: Gateways whose \fBgatewayClassName\fR is \fBclass\fR and the HTTPRoutes whose \fBparentRefs\fR name them translate as well. Route hostnames come from the HTTPRoute or, when it has none, from the parent listeners\(aq hostnames (wildcards allowed). Each rule and match becomes a route \fBk8s\-gw\-<namespace>\-<httproute>\-<rule>\-<match>\fR: \fBPathPrefix\fR and \fBExact\fR paths (priority 10 for exact), \fBRegularExpression\fR paths as \fBpath_regex\fR, a \fBmethod\fR match, and header matches of type \fBExact\fR and \fBRegularExpression\fR as \fBheaders\fR conditions (a match with an unknown header match type or a pattern that does not compile is skipped with a warning). Filters: \fBRequestHeaderModifier\fR and \fBResponseHeaderModifier\fR become header operations, \fBURLRewrite\fR with \fBReplaceFullPath\fR becomes \fBrewrite_path\fR, with \fBReplacePrefixMatch: /\fR \fBstrip_prefix\fR, and a \fBhostname\fR \fBhost_header\fR; \fBRequestRedirect\fR with a \fBhostname\fR becomes a redirect action (a redirect without a hostname is not supported). A rule with one backend uses that service; several \fBbackendRefs\fR become one \fBweighted\fR upstream over all their endpoints with the reference weights (weight 0 excluded). Listener \fBcertificateRefs\fR install the secrets like Ingress TLS. \fBGET /v1/ingress\fR and \fBxproxyctl ingress\fR show syncs, errors, watch streams and events, counts (Ingresses, Gateways, HTTPRoutes, routes, upstreams, certificates) and the translation warnings. \fBdeploy/kubernetes/xproxy.yaml\fR is a complete deployment with RBAC, an IngressClass and a ConfigMap; \fBdeploy/kubernetes/Containerfile\fR builds the image.
.SH "metrics"
.PP
The management socket always serves \fB/metrics\fR in Prometheus text format and \fB/v1/series\fR with sampled series. This section adds an optional TCP endpoint for scrapers and sizes the series buffer.
.PP
.TS
