.SS "routes[].static"
.PP
A \fBstatic\fR route serves files from a directory: assets next to an application, a maintenance page, a single page application. The request path after \fBstrip_prefix\fR or \fBrewrite_path\fR selects the file. Files are opened through \fBos.Root\fR, so neither \fB..\fR (removed earlier by path cleaning) nor a symbolic link pointing outside the root can leave it; names starting with a dot (\fB.env\fR, \fB.git\fR) are refused unless \fBdot_files\fR is set; anything that is not a regular file or directory answers 404, as does every failure to open, so the tree\(aqs shape leaks nothing. \fBGET\fR and \fBHEAD\fR only (405 otherwise). Responses carry a weak \fBETag\fR from size and modification time, honour \fBIf\-None\-Match\fR, \fBIf\-Modified\-Since\fR and \fBRange\fR, and set the content type from a fixed table for the common web types (\fBtext/javascript\fR, \fBtext/css\fR, \fBimage/svg+xml\fR, \fBapplication/wasm\fR, ...) with \fBX\-Content\-Type\-Options: nosniff\fR. A directory without a trailing slash redirects to it (301), then serves \fBindex\fR, then a listing when enabled, else 404. The route\(aqs admission pipeline (bans, limits, ACLs, WAF, filters) applies before the file is opened, and \fBresponse_headers\fR apply to every answer.
.PP
.TS
