.SH "icap"
.PP
Present means scanning services are available; routes opt in with an \fBicap\fR block. Requests (REQMOD) and responses (RESPMOD) are handed to the service per RFC 3507 with preview and \fB204 No Content\fR support. A \fB200\fR answer with an encapsulated response is sent to the client as is (a block page); one with an encapsulated request replaces the method, path, headers and body sent upstream, except the protected headers (\fBHost\fR, the forwarding headers, \fBAuthorization\fR, \fBCookie\fR).
.SS "icap.services[]"
.PP
.TS
