Orders use a fresh P\-256 key per certificate and an ES256 account key. A certificate is installed only after the returned chain is verified to cover every host in the group. Status is at \fBGET /v1/acme\fR and \fBxproxyctl acme\fR; \fBxproxyctl acme renew\fR forces renewal of every group and waits for the outcome (a renewal already running is joined, not duplicated).
.SH "shedding"
.PP
Present means enabled. The load level is the larger of the in\-flight ratio (\fBin_flight / max_concurrent_requests\fR) and the latency level (\fB(latency \- target) / target\fR, capped at 1, where latency is the average upstream time to first byte over \fBwindow\fR). A class is shed with 503 while the level is at or above its threshold and admitted again once the level falls below the threshold minus \fBhysteresis\fR. Critical routes are never shed. A window without samples drains the latency signal, so shedding never locks in.
.PP
.TS
