.SS "challenge.captcha"
.PP
Adds a second tier to the challenge. A verdict that asks for it (an \fBaccount_guard\fR step or \fBdisposable\fR action \fBcaptcha\fR, a \fBdistributed\fR action \fBcaptcha\fR) renders the provider\(aqs widget instead of the proof of work; a client that solved only the proof of work is challenged again, and a client that passed the CAPTCHA satisfies both tiers. The token is verified with the provider from the proxy (\fBsiteverify\fR, with the client address), fails closed when the provider is unreachable or rejects it, and the failure is a \fBchallenge_failed\fR security event naming the class (\fBcaptcha rejected\fR, \fBcaptcha score\fR, \fBcaptcha unreachable\fR). The page\(aqs Content Security Policy admits the provider\(aqs script and frame origins only. Without this section a CAPTCHA verdict falls back to the proof of work.
.PP
